{
  "score": 7.5,
  "flaws": [
    "Trajectory smoothness and gate centering: Although all 16/16 trials pass, the flight path is noticeably jerky rather than smooth. In the top and low views, there are sharp angular kinks before Gate 1, after Gate 2, and during the final descent (which wobbles in an S-curve above the landing pad). In the chase view, the trajectory passes dangerously close to the right vertical post of Gate 3 instead of flying cleanly through the center.",
    "Flight path tube visibility: The flight path is rendered as a razor-thin line with small beads rather than a substantial, easy-to-read 3D tube, making it hard to inspect trajectory curvature and clearance at a glance.",
    "3D label collisions and low-contrast typography: In the chase view, the floating 'LAND' label intersects directly with the quadcopter's right rotors. In the low camera view, 'GATE 1', 'GATE 2', and 'GATE 3' stack on top of one another and the gate frames, while 'TAKE-OFF' is washed out and barely legible against the grey floor.",
    "UI text formatting and camera framing: In the top-left info card, the stats string is missing punctuation/spacing between '12.91 s flight' and 'Landing error 0.027 m.' Additionally, the top-down camera frames the room at a 45-degree diamond angle that clips the top and bottom corners of the room boundary off-screen."
  ],
  "summary": "Strong engineering baseline with 16/16 validation trials passing in under 13 seconds and low landing error (0.027 m). However, to reach a 9+/10, the controller needs smoother trajectory generation and better wind rejection so it flies cleanly through the center of each gate without sharp kinks or landing-descent oscillations, alongside visual polish for the path tube thickness, 3D label placement, and UI text formatting."
}

